A linked list is a chain of nodes. Each node holds a value and a reference to the next node, and the last node's `next` is `null`. Define the node class after `Main`:

```java
class ListNode {
    int val;
    ListNode next;
    ListNode(int val) {
        this.val = val;
    }
}
System.out.println(new ListNode(5).next); // null
```

To build a list in input order, start from a **dummy head** and keep a `tail` pointer. Each new node hangs off `tail`, then `tail` moves onto it. The real list starts at `dummy.next`.

