Walk a list with `while (cur != null)` and `cur = cur.next`. Forget that last line and the loop never ends. To print `1 -> 2 -> 3`, append each value to a `StringBuilder` and add the arrow only when `cur.next != null`.

Unlike an array, there is no `list[i]`: reaching position i means walking i steps. Java also ships `java.util.LinkedList`, which is both a `List` and a `Deque`. Here you build your own nodes to learn how they work.

